[Round 2/3 | Implementer | 186.1s | 0/400k] The first ring-window measurement exposed the key bottleneck: the queue reaches near capacity, so “scan the live window” still means roughly 1024 slot inspections per dequeue. I’m switching the exact SPSC fast path to a two-ring index exchange plus a consumer-local binary min-heap. Enqueues only take one free index; dequeues drain newly published indices into the heap and pop the minimum. The old authoritative bitmap/state scan remains the fallback for non-SPSC or any metadata inconsistency.

